  ex:l6-crm-chart a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:DotPlot ; skos:prefLabel "Independent recovery preparations"@en ; cd:body "Each dot is one independent synthetic preparation; repeated values stay separate. Mean recovery: 101.5%, versus fixed target 100%. With independent Normal results: t = 3.503, df 5, two-sided p = 0.0172. At 5%, reject equality; the estimated departure is +1.5 percentage points, not automatically an important bias."@en ; cd:xAxisLabel "Sampling unit"@en ; cd:yAxisLabel "Recovery"@en ; cd:yAxisUnit "%" ; cd:hasChartGroup ex:l6-crm-group ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-paired-chart a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:DotPlot ; skos:prefLabel "Same sites at two times: one difference per site"@en ; cd:body "Separate synthetic concentration case, not diclofenac: each dot is a site's before-minus-after change; zero stays. Mean decrease 2.833 mg/L. Independent Normal differences: paired t = 4.029, df 5, two-sided p = 0.0100. At 5%, reject zero mean change; the before/after design alone does not establish its cause."@en ; cd:xAxisLabel "Independent site pairs"@en ; cd:yAxisLabel "Before minus after"@en ; cd:yAxisUnit "mg/L" ; cd:hasChartGroup ex:l6-pair-group ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-welch-chart a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:DotPlot ; skos:prefLabel "Separate assay example: independent vessels"@en ; cd:body "Generic assay response in arbitrary units, not algal growth rate. One dot per independent synthetic vessel; means 10 and 15 a.u. Control minus exposure: −5 a.u. Welch gives t = −2.970, approximate df 6.972, two-sided p = 0.0209. At 5%, reject equal means under the independent Normal-group model. Higher response alone does not establish toxicity."@en ; cd:xAxisLabel "Independent vessel group"@en ; cd:yAxisLabel "Assay response"@en ; cd:yAxisUnit "a.u." ; cd:hasChartGroup ex:l6-control-group, ex:l6-exposure-group ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-anova-chart a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:DotPlot ; skos:prefLabel "Three synthetic exposure groups"@en ; cd:body "Three independent synthetic vessels per group; means 5, 8 and 11 a.u. Differences between means are large relative to scatter within groups. Under independent Normal errors with a common variance: F = 27, df (2, 6), p = 0.001. Reject equal population means at 5%; planned adjusted follow-ups ask which groups differ."@en ; cd:xAxisLabel "Exposure group"@en ; cd:yAxisLabel "Vessel response"@en ; cd:yAxisUnit "a.u." ; cd:hasChartGroup ex:l6-anova-group-a, ex:l6-anova-group-b, ex:l6-anova-group-c ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-grubbs-chart a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:DotPlot ; skos:prefLabel "Retain the high nitrate preparation"@en ; cd:body "The 12.5 mg/L result stays visible with the other five synthetic preparations. Grubbs statistic 2.0219 exceeds the two-sided 5% cutoff 1.8871 under the single-outlier Normal model. Flag it and investigate its origin. The test does not identify an error or justify automatic deletion."@en ; cd:xAxisLabel "Independent preparations"@en ; cd:yAxisLabel "Nitrate"@en ; cd:yAxisUnit "mg/L" ; cd:hasChartGroup ex:l6-grubbs-group ; cd:authoredResource true .
